# ShadowMain / ShadowBackup — identical mirror

ShadowSyn runs **active-active** on two Discord guilds. **ShadowBackup must identically mirror ShadowMain** in structure, behavior, and user-facing content. This applies to **all Discord server work and all ShadowSyn bot work** — code, channels, threads, roles, embeds, hub panels, deploy commands, scripts, and ops.

| Name | Guild ID | Role |
|------|----------|------|
| **ShadowMain** | `908659586536468540` | Primary production community |
| **ShadowBackup** | `1514838718119411832` | Identical mirrored failover (shdwbackup) |

## Mirror mandate (non-negotiable)

When anything changes on **ShadowMain**, **ShadowBackup must receive the same change** in the **same task** unless Joseph explicitly opts out in chat.

**Forbidden without explicit opt-out:**
- "Main only for v1"
- Hardcoding `SHADOW_MAIN_GUILD_ID` in deploy scripts (default must be `--guild all`)
- Shipping a registry key on Main but not Backup
- Deploying a panel/hub on one guild only

This includes:

- **Bot code** — one code path; both guilds via `REGISTERED_GUILD_IDS` and `guild_registry` keys
- **Discord structure** — new/renamed channels, categories, threads, roles on Main → replicate on Backup → `python scripts/guild_registry_seed.py`
- **Panels & hubs** — deploy on **both** guilds (see checklist below)
- **Embeds & copy** — same titles, descriptions, colors (`#2B0B35`), buttons; no Main-only messaging
- **Slash commands & bindings** — deploy/admin commands on **both** guilds
- **Scripts & Cursor ops** — ShadowAdmin audits and deploy helpers default to **both** guilds

